# FinScope — environment template
#
# FinScope is a frontend-only demo. The current source reads **no** environment
# variables: there is no backend URL, no API key, no broker token and no
# database connection. All market data, news and calendar events are
# deterministic synthetic fixtures under src/mocks/.
#
# You do not need to create a .env file to run the project:
#
#   npm install
#   npm run dev
#
# User preferences (theme, market colours, default asset class, default chart
# range, number format, base currency) are persisted in localStorage via
# Zustand — see src/store/settings.ts — not in environment files.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# House rules for future configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables are exposed to the browser and they are
#    public by definition. Never place secrets in this file.
# 2. Anything that could be a credential (API key, broker token, database
#    password) must not be added — this project intentionally has no backend
#    and no authenticated data source.
# 3. If a build-time constant becomes necessary, document it here with its
#    default value and the file that consumes it.
